@startuml Topic6_Subagent_Design
' ============================================================
' TOPIC 6: Subagent Design (the workers)
' MOST TESTED: CONTEXT ISOLATION — subagent starts BLANK.
' Single Responsibility Principle. Least privilege on tools.
' ============================================================
title Topic 6 — Subagent Design\n(Own context + own tools; CONTEXT ISOLATION is the most-tested idea)

skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 12

start

:Orchestrator needs a subtask done;

#LightCyan:Spin up a SUBAGENT;
note right
  Each subagent owns:
  * its OWN context window
  * its OWN tool permissions
end note

partition "CONTEXT ISOLATION (most-tested)" {
  :Subagent starts BLANK;
  note right
    It inherits NOTHING automatically.
    Any fact it needs must be EXPLICITLY
    passed in by the orchestrator.
  end note
  if (How much context to pass?) then (Goldilocks test)
    :Pass the MINIMUM NECESSARY context;
    note right
      * Too little  -> underpowered, guesses, fails
      * Too much    -> bloat, cost, noise, leakage
      * Just right  -> minimal but sufficient
    end note
  endif
}

partition "LEAST PRIVILEGE (tools)" {
  :Grant ONLY the tools this job needs;
  note right
    Tool permissions = an AUTHORITY boundary.
    Fewer tools = smaller blast radius.
  end note
}

partition "GOOD INSTRUCTIONS need 3 things" {
  :1. Narrow SCOPE (one job);
  :2. OUTPUT FORMAT (what to return);
  :3. SUCCESS CRITERIA (what "done" means);
}

if (Can you describe the job in ONE sentence\nwith defined input + output?) then (YES)
  #LightGreen:Well-designed subagent\n(substitutable + testable);
else (NO — too broad)
  #Pink:ANTI-PATTERN — scope too broad;
  note right
    Three anti-patterns:
    1. Broad scope (does too many things)
    2. Underpowered context (starved of facts)
    3. Unclear success criteria (never knows when done)
  end note
endif

stop

floating note left
  == MENTAL MODEL: SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY PRINCIPLE ==
  One subagent = ONE job, ONE goal.
  (Like a well-designed function/class.)
  ....
  Benefits of context isolation:
  * prevents context bloat
  * limits information leakage
  * reduces cost
  * makes each subagent independently TESTABLE
  ----
  Analogies:
  * least privilege  ~ limited access
  * context isolation ~ no shared global state
end note

@enduml
